  "findings": [
    "With explicit 25 C operating temperature and nominal 27 C, Xyce reproduces the large ground-loaded branch separation for both candidate models at both sweep resolutions.",
    "The sink-RE10 supply-loaded tied-input case also appears direction-independent at 1 mV resolution but exposes a branch difference at the intermediate 0.5 mV sample in Xyce.",
    "All corrected per-case output differences between solvers are below 3 mV. This is a reported observation, not a declared acceptance tolerance or proof that default device equations are identical.",
    "The repeated branch behavior is evidence against an ngspice-only operating-point artifact; it directs further work toward model applicability and transition-region characteristics."
  ],
